# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions. Written 2026-11-22.
# UCI general rules for unknown tokens, whitespace and line endings.
> unknown
> unknown\tisready\t
# UCI isready/readyok after skipping the unknown line and prefix.
< readyok
>    isready\r
# UCI arbitrary whitespace and CRLF line endings.
< readyok
>CR isready
# UCI allows CR alone as a command terminator.
< readyok
> setoption name Path value caf\xe9
> isready
# The owner ignores setoption. UCI isready/readyok verifies that input continues.
< readyok
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
